.TH "GCON-PROBE" 7 "Gcon test" "Gcon" "Gcon documentation"
.SH NAME
\&The probe page
\&Every construct of the documentation's Markdown, for the renderers' golden files: \fIemphasis\fR, \fBstrong\fR, \fBcode with \-flags\fR, a backslash * for a literal star, a page, a heading, and a URL <https://example.com/x?a=1&b=2>. Escaped: <, &, "quotes", a backslash \e and a leading .dot that roff must not take as a request.
.SH "LISTS"
.IP \(bu 4
\&one item, whose text runs on for long enough that it has to be filled onto a second line in the text renderer
.IP \(bu 4
\&two, with \fBcode\fR
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 4
\&nested, level one
.IP \(bu 4
\&nested again
.RE
.IP "" 4
\&A paragraph inside the second item.
.IP "" 4
.RS 4
.nf
\&code inside the item
.fi
.RE
.IP \(bu 4
\&three
.IP "1." 4
\&first
.IP "2." 4
\&second
.IP "3." 4
\&third
.SH "CODE"
.RS 4
.nf
\&procedure main()
\&   write("hello, \e"world\e" <&>")   # a comment
\&end
.fi
.RE
.SS "A table"
.RS 4
.nf
\&Name  Meaning
\&----  -------------
\&-raw  the Markdown
\&-man  roff, for man
.fi
.RE
.SS "Smallest heading"
\&Repeated heading:
.SH "LISTS"
\&The end.
